# {{name}}

A Pterodactyl panel language pack for `{{language}}`, scaffolded by `p:extension:make --language={{language}}`.
It has no PHP provider and no frontend build: the panel reads its translation files directly.

## Files

| File | |
| --- | --- |
| `extension.json` | The manifest. `"languages": ["{{language}}"]` lists the locales this pack provides. |
| `resources/languages/{{language}}.json` | The panel's interface text, keyed by the English. Translate the values and keep the keys. |
| `resources/languages/{{language}}/*.php` | Copies of the panel's English server messages (validation, emails, activity log). Translate the values and keep the keys. |

Placeholders must be kept as they are: `{{user}}` in the JSON file, `:user` in the PHP files. Plural forms use
`_one` and `_other` suffixes (`{{count}} file_one`, `{{count}} file_other`); add the other forms the language
needs, such as `_few` or `_many`.

Any key left out falls back to English, so a pack can translate part of the panel and grow over time. A
file only needs the keys it translates. Extensions add their interface text to the same JSON catalogue, so
`{{language}}.json` translates them too. To translate another extension's server messages, add
`resources/languages/vendor/ext-<id>/{{language}}/<group>.php` with that extension's keys.

When two enabled packs provide the same key for a locale, the one loaded later wins: a pack listed under
`requires.extensions` loads first, and unrelated packs load in alphabetical order.
`p:lang:coverage` and the Admin API's extension listing (`language_conflicts`) report such conflicts.

## Develop

```sh
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --enable
php {{artisan}} p:lang:coverage {{language}} --extension={{id}}
php {{artisan}} p:extension:pack .
```

`p:lang:coverage` lists missing and stale keys, values still the same as the English, and placeholder
mistakes. It exits non-zero when keys are missing or a translation uses a placeholder English does not. The
scaffolded files start as copies of the English, so every key is listed as the same as English until it is
translated.
